From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:58:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 551/551] [DS4.1] IKET debug mode: phase ranges in every
 TileLang kernel (VLLM_DS41_IKET)

VLLM_DS41_IKET=<directory> turns on, for the worker process, a pass over every
TileLang kernel's generated CUDA that wraps its load, wait, compute and store
phases in IKET ranges (TileLang's tilelang.tools.cuda.iket). Kernel sources are
unchanged. Off, nothing is imported and no TileLang callback is registered.
On, TileLang's caches are off and kept under the directory, so no instrumented
kernel reaches the deployment's cache; kernels still declare, prepare and freeze.
Traces need NVIDIA's run-iket profiler (CuTe DSL).
